Here is a basic Unity C# script that moves a player and allows them to jump:

``` 
using System.Collections;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using UnityEngine;

public class PlayerController : MonoBehaviour
{
    public float speed;
    public float jumpHeight;
    public Transform jumpObject;

    private float jumpTime;
    private float movementTime;

    void Update()
    {
        // Check if the player is moving
        if (Input.GetKeyDown(KeyCode.E))
        {
            // If the player is moving, update their speed
             movementTime = Input.GetTime(KeyCode.E);
            Vector3 movement = new Vector3( movementTime.x, 0, 0);
            transform.Translate( movement * speed * Time.deltaTime);
        }

        // Check if the player is about to jump
        if (Input.GetKeyDown(KeyCode.S))
        {
            // If the player is about to jump, update their height
             jumpHeight = Input.GetTime(KeyCode.S) * jumpHeight;
             jumpObject.position = jumpObject.position + jumpHeight * Time.deltaTime;
        }

        // Check if the player has finished moving
        if (Input.GetKeyDown(KeyCode.E))
        {
            // If the player has finished moving, update their speed
             movementTime = Input.GetTime(KeyCode.E);
            Vector3 movement = new Vector3( movementTime.x, 0, 0);
            transform.Translate( movement * speed * Time.deltaTime);
        }
    }
}
```

This script uses the `Input.GetKeyDown()` method to check if the player is moving at all. If they are, it updates their speed and translation.

The `Input.GetTime()` method allows you to check how long it has been since the player was last moved. If the player is about to jump, it updates their height and jumpObject\'s position.

Finally, the `Update()` method is called every frame in Unity. In this method, you can update the player\'s speed and position, and check if they are about to jump or not.

Note that this script only allows the player to jump if they are being moved by the keyboard. If you want to allow the player to jump even if they are not moving, you will need to add a new function to the `Update()` method that checks if the player is standing still and then allows them to jump.

